    {
      "title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a92c0a9e109cec8e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWalter Frederick Ferrier - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a92c0a9e109cec8e\">>>",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Frederick_Ferrier",
      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"399813de2e5ac961\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIt turned out to be a new member of the Zeolite family of minerals. Subsequently, it was named after him - Ferrierite. The type material of this mineral is stored at the Redpath Museum and is part of a separate collection that also bears his name. L.S. Stevenson, &quot;Walter F.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"399813de2e5ac961\">>>",
      "published": "February 14, 2022",
      "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"
    },
    {
      "title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"80ca4430c773e00c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFerrierite Subgroup: Mineral information, data and localities.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"80ca4430c773e00c\">>>",
      "url": "https://www.mindat.org/min-1492.html",
      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dd90797acd9647e4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFerrier ... Named in 1918 by Richard Percival Devereux Graham in honor of Walter Frederick Ferrier [4 May 1865 Montréal, Québec, Canada – 15 November 1950 Toronto, York County, Ontario, Canada], mineralogist, mining engineer, and geologist with the Geological Survey of Canada, who first collected the material on the north shore of Kamloops Lake, British Columbia, Canada.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dd90797acd9647e4\">>>",
      "published": "February 15, 2025",
      "siteName": "www.mindat.org"
    },
    {
      "title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5309f2232b703e1e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n30 Facts About Ferrierite - Facts.net\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5309f2232b703e1e\">>>",
      "url": "https://facts.net/earth-and-life-science/earth-sciences/30-facts-about-ferrierite/",
      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"92491e3656e0cd23\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nBut what exactly makes Ferrierite so special? This mineral is <strong>composed of a framework of silicon, aluminum, and oxygen atoms</strong>, creating a porous structure that can trap and release molecules.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"92491e3656e0cd23\">>>",
      "published": "December 4, 2024",
      "siteName": "facts.net"
    }
  ]
